<title>UK: GM weak in London on profits warning talk.</title>
<headline>GM weak in London on profits warning talk.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in General Motors were under pressure in Europe on Thursday on talk that the U.S. automaker had issued a profits warning, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;GM could have a rough time on Wall Street today,&quot; one dealer said. &quot;They're talking about a 40 percent profits shortfall.&quot;</p>
<p>Dealers in London, citing press reports, said GM had warned Q4 earnings would be around $0.60 a share compared with market expectations of $1.00-$1.10.</p>
<p>GM shares were down $5/8 at $53-7/8 by 1140 GMT.</p>
<p>-- Dale Faulken, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
